  'ls.sow.title': 'How sowing works', 'ls.sow.sub': 'Count where the last seed stops', 'ls.sow.goal': 'Make your last seed stop on the gold dotted target.',
  'ls.sow.intro': '<p>Pick a pit, take all its seeds and sow them one by one <b>counter-clockwise</b>: left to right along the bottom row, into your store, then right to left along the top row.</p><p>Where the last seed stops decides extra turns and captures. Remember: <b>a pit with n seeds moves n places</b>.</p><p class="note">Your opponent\'s store is skipped. With 7 or more seeds you reach the other row; 13 seeds go exactly once around.</p>',
  'ls.sow.why': 'Pit {m} holds exactly as many seeds as the distance to the target.', 'ls.sow.hint': 'Count the places up to the target (your store counts as one) and find the pit with that many seeds.',
  'ls.extra.title': 'Land in your store', 'ls.extra.sub': 'Exact count = extra turn', 'ls.extra.goal': 'Find the best move.',
  'ls.extra.intro': '<p>If the last seed drops into <b>your store</b>, you move again.</p><p>Look for a pit whose <b>seed count equals its distance to the store</b>: 1 in pit 6, 2 in pit 5, 3 in pit 4…</p><p class="note">An extra turn wins a seed and a tempo — the most important move in Mancala.</p>',
  'ls.extra.why': 'Pit {m} reaches your store exactly, so you move again.', 'ls.extra.hint': 'Which pit has as many seeds as its distance to the store? If there are several, start with the one closest to the store.',
  'ls.capture.title': 'Captures', 'ls.capture.sub': 'Stop in an empty pit, take the seeds opposite', 'ls.capture.goal': 'Find the best move.',
  'ls.capture.intro': '<p>If your last seed stops in an <b>empty pit on your side</b> and the opposite pit holds seeds, you put <b>those seeds and your last seed</b> into your store (Kalah).</p><p>When a big pile of your opponent\'s faces an empty pit of yours, look for a move that stops there.</p><p class="note">A pit with 13 seeds goes all the way round and stops in its own, now empty, pit.</p>',
  'ls.capture.why': 'Pit {m} stops in an empty pit and captures the seeds opposite.', 'ls.capture.hint': 'Red rings mark opponent seeds facing an empty pit of yours. Which pit makes your last seed stop there?',
  'ls.defend.title': 'Stop the capture', 'ls.defend.sub': 'Protect a pile under attack', 'ls.defend.goal': 'Your opponent threatens a capture. Find the best move.',
  'ls.defend.intro': '<p>Always check whether one of your piles <b>can be captured</b> on your opponent\'s next move: if their last seed stops in an empty pit on their side, <b>your pile</b> opposite is taken.</p><p>Three ways to defend: <b>① move the threatened pile</b>, <b>② fill the empty pit they would land in</b>, <b>③ add seeds to their pit so it stops somewhere else</b>.</p>',
  'ls.defend.why': 'Pit {m} defuses your opponent\'s capture.', 'ls.defend.hint': 'Red rings mark your seeds that the opponent could capture next move.',
  'ls.chain.title': 'Chain extra turns', 'ls.chain.sub': 'The right order for many extra turns', 'ls.chain.goal': 'Which first move starts the longest chain?',
  'ls.chain.intro': '<p>Several extra turns <b>in a row</b> gain a lot.</p><p>The trick is to start <b>with the pit closest to your store</b>. Sowing a far pit first adds a seed to the near pits, so they no longer fit exactly.</p><p class="note">Sowing can also make another pit fit exactly. Read the chain ahead.</p>',
  'ls.chain.why': 'Starting with pit {m} gives the longest chain of extra turns.', 'ls.chain.hint': 'Work from the store outwards and look for exact counts. Moving a far pit first changes the near ones.',
  'ls.endgame.title': 'Count and hoard', 'ls.endgame.sub': 'Count the endgame, keep seeds in your row', 'ls.endgame.goal': 'Read to the end and find the best move.',
  'ls.endgame.intro': '<p>Endgames <b>can be counted out</b>. More than half of all seeds in your store decides the game (25 with 4 seeds per pit).</p><p>When a row runs empty, <b>the remaining seeds belong to the owner of each row</b>. Seeds you <b>hoard</b> in your row become yours at the end; if your row empties first, everything left on the other side goes to your opponent.</p><p class="note">This step is scored with a perfect, solved-to-the-end evaluation.</p>',
  'ls.endgame.why': 'Pit {m} is the best move with perfect play.', 'ls.endgame.hint': 'After each move, count your opponent\'s best reply. Seeds left in your row become yours at the end.',
  'pz.title': 'Puzzles', 'pz.desc': 'Every puzzle is verified by the engine and has exactly one correct first move. Five levels of 20 puzzles, plus a new daily puzzle every day.',
  'pz.retry': 'Retry', 'pz.answer': 'Answer', 'pz.next': 'Next', 'pz.list': 'List',
  'pz.max': 'Maximum haul', 'pz.max.d': 'Put as many seeds as possible in your store this turn', 'pz.chain': 'Chains', 'pz.chain.d': 'Find the order that chains three or more extra turns',
  'pz.end': 'Endgame', 'pz.end.d': 'Up to 12 seeds left; play perfectly against a perfect defender', 'pz.end2': 'Endgame · advanced', 'pz.end2.d': '13–18 seeds left; a longer fight', 'pz.relay': 'Sunka relays', 'pz.relay.d': 'Win a huge haul with relay sowing (Sunka rules)',
  'pz.goalTurn': 'Put at least <b>{n} seeds</b> into your store this turn.', 'pz.goalEnd': 'Finish <b>{a} − {b}</b> (the best possible) against perfect play.',
  'pz.startTurn': 'You are the bottom row. Keep moving as long as you earn extra turns.', 'pz.startEnd': 'You are the bottom row. Your opponent replies perfectly; a single inferior move fails.',
  'pz.failTurn': 'Pit {m} gets at most {n} seeds (goal {g}).', 'pz.failEnd': 'Pit {m} falls short of the best result.', 'pz.bestWas': 'The gold ring is the answer (pit {m}).',
  'pz.fail': 'Failed', 'pz.good': 'Correct!', 'pz.again': 'Extra turn! {n} more seeds.', 'pz.yourMove': 'Your move.', 'pz.opp': 'Opponent is thinking…', 'pz.checking': 'Checking…', 'pz.solved': 'Solved!',
